{# Render every entry of the SAI_PROFILE CONFIG_DB table as a KEY=VALUE
   line. This is a generic, vendor-agnostic include: it makes no
   assumption about which keys are present, so it can be reused
   unmodified by any hwsku's sai.profile.j2, across vendors.

   This file lives under sonic-config-engine's data/ dir (not
   files/build_templates/) so setup.py's data_files glob installs it
   into /usr/share/sonic/templates as part of the sonic-config-engine
   package itself. That is what makes it resolve inside containers
   such as syncd (built FROM docker-config-engine-trixie, which
   installs this package), not just on the host rootfs where
   sai.profile.j2 is not actually rendered.

   Defense-in-depth: YANG validation (the key-name pattern, the
   reserved-key "must" constraint, and the value's CR/LF-excluding
   pattern) only applies to config changes made through the
   YANG-validated path. A direct sonic-db-cli write to CONFIG_DB
   bypasses YANG, so the same guards are re-applied here:
   - A key containing '=', CR, or LF is dropped entirely: consumers
     that split each line on the first '=' would otherwise
     mis-parse a key like "SAI_INIT_CONFIG_FILE=/tmp/evil" (with
     value "x") as the reserved key SAI_INIT_CONFIG_FILE with value
     "/tmp/evil=x", and CR/LF in a key can inject another profile
     line exactly like CR/LF in a value can.
   - SAI_INIT_CONFIG_FILE is reserved/structural (selected by each
     platform's sai.profile.j2) and is never emitted from this table.
   - CR/LF in a value is stripped so one entry can never expand into
     more than one KEY=VALUE line. #}
{%- if SAI_PROFILE is defined %}
{%- for key, entry in SAI_PROFILE.items() %}
{%- if key != 'SAI_INIT_CONFIG_FILE'
      and (key | replace('=', '') | replace('\r', '') | replace('\n', '')) == key %}
{{ key }}={{ entry.value | replace('\r', '') | replace('\n', ' ') }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
